# ** VHF 8 NOTE - June 2026 **
# According to ACMA (Australian Communications and Media Authority), two different frequencies
# (191.5Mhz and 191.625Mhz) are used for channel VHF 8.  191.625Mhz was selected for use in
# this file because even though transmitters using 191.5Mhz are more numerous,
# transmitters using 191.625Mhz appear to represent the highest population coverage.
# Both of these frequencies tuned correctly when tested in Sydney (a 191.625Mhz location)!
# Most other channels share this issue, albeit to a lesser extent.
# Providing both frequencies (like in auto-Australia) results in duplicated services.
#

